        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 80-year-old male patient, admitted on 14/04/2018 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, physical examination revealed reduced air entry bilaterally with expiratory wheeze. Oxygen saturation was diminished at room air. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation consistent with COPD without evidence of pneumonia or pneumothorax. Blood tests revealed mild inflammatory markers. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and intravenous fluids. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. Discharge was arranged on 15/04/2018 with optimised inhaler regimen and outpatient follow-up arranged. Please ensure ongoing COPD monitoring and medication review at your earliest convenience.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "8648-8",
